rustbcx

This crate is a port to Rust of the works below. It is offered as a whole under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

1. bc7e.ispc, the BC7 texture encoder by Binomial LLC (src/bc7e.rs):

    bc7e.ispc - Fast high quality SIMD BC7 encoder
    Copyright (C) 2018-2020 Binomial LLC, All rights reserved. Apache 2.0 license.

   taken from Richard Geldreich's bc7enc_rdo (https://github.com/richgel999/bc7enc_rdo), which
   holds its latest version; the original release is https://github.com/BinomialLLC/bc7e.

   The original is changed here in that it is translated from ISPC to Rust: it packs one block
   at a time where the original packs several side by side, its start-up tables are a value
   and not globals, and its settings and entry points have Rust's names. What it computes is
   kept: it gives the same blocks as the original built without fast-math and without fused
   multiply-add.

2. bc7enc_rdo, by Richard Geldreich, Jr. (https://github.com/richgel999/bc7enc_rdo): its
   bc7decomp.cpp, bc7enc.cpp, rgbcx.cpp, ert.cpp and rdo_bc_encoder.cpp with their headers
   and tables, and the parts of utils.h and utils.cpp those use (src/bc7decomp.rs,
   src/bc7enc.rs, src/rgbcx.rs, src/rgbcx_tables.rs, src/ert.rs, src/rdo_bc_encoder.rs,
   src/image.rs).

    Copyright(c) 2020-2021 Richard Geldreich, Jr.

   Those files are offered by their author under the MIT licence or as public domain
   (unlicense.org), whichever the user prefers; that notice is kept in LICENSE-bc7enc_rdo.txt.

   They are changed here in that they are translated from C++ to Rust: the tables the C++
   keeps in globals are values, and the entry points have Rust's names. What they compute is
   kept: they give the same blocks as the C++ library.

3. bcdec, by Sergii Kudlai (https://github.com/iOrange/bcdec): the BC6H unpacker of its
   bcdec.h (in src/bc6h.rs).

    Copyright (c) 2022 Sergii Kudlai

   That file is offered by its author under the MIT licence or as public domain
   (unlicense.org), whichever the user prefers; that notice is kept in LICENSE-bcdec.txt. It
   is changed here in that it is translated from C to Rust and gives its pixels back as a
   value. What it computes is kept.

4. The ISPC Texture Compressor, by Intel Corporation
   (https://github.com/GameTechDev/ISPCTextureCompressor): the BC6H encoder of its
   ispc_texcomp/kernel.ispc, with the helpers it shares with that file's BC7 encoder, and
   the five BC6H profiles of ispc_texcomp.cpp (in src/bc6h.rs).

    Copyright 2017 Intel Corporation

   Those files are under the MIT licence; that notice is kept in LICENSE-ispc-texcomp.txt.
   They are changed here in that they are translated from ISPC and C++ to Rust: one block is
   packed at a time where the original packs several side by side, and the settings and
   entry points have Rust's names. What they compute is kept: the same blocks as the
   original built without fast-math and without fused multiply-add.

5. bc6h_enc, by Alexander Samusev (https://github.com/0xc0de/bc6h_enc), which is the BC6H
   encoder of DirectXTex, by Microsoft (https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTex,
   BC6HBC7.cpp), made into one file: the encoder of its bc6h_enc.h, with its tables
   (src/bc6h_enc.rs, src/bc6h_enc_tables.rs).

    Copyright (c) 2022 Alexander Samusev
    Copyright (c) 2011-2022 Microsoft Corp

   Both are under the MIT licence; those notices are kept in LICENSE-bc6h_enc.txt. The file
   is changed here in that it is translated from C++ to Rust, and its decoder is left out.
   What it computes is kept: the same blocks as the original built with
   BC6H_SSE_INTRINSICS.

What is around the ports is the crate's own: mip levels and the HDR image (in src/image.rs),
float_to_half (in src/bc6h.rs), src/bc2.rs (BC2, its colours packed and unpacked by the
port of rgbcx), BC2 in src/rdo_bc_encoder.rs, src/texture.rs,
src/dds.rs (its writer after bc7enc_rdo's save_dds), src/ktx.rs and src/parallel.rs. The
data format descriptor src/ktx.rs writes into a .ktx2 file follows the one the Khronos
Group's KTX-Software writes (createDFDCompressed in its dfdutils, Apache 2.0).

The port was made in 2026 for the Noolith project.
